WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.350
Weak offers hide in vague promises, fuzzy who, and missing next steps.

00:00:04.350 --> 00:00:06.887
This lesson is about offer critique clinic.

00:00:06.887 --> 00:00:07.975
Common weak offers.

00:00:07.975 --> 00:00:10.512
Do not treat this as theory only.

00:00:10.512 --> 00:00:14.137
Treat it as a move you can run this week.

00:00:14.137 --> 00:00:19.575
By the end, you should be able to act without waiting for a perfect plan.

00:00:19.575 --> 00:00:23.562
Keep the DigProg habit: watch, practice, then take one real action.

00:00:23.562 --> 00:00:27.912
Stay practical: fix three weak lines before you optimize branding or tools.

00:00:28.232 --> 00:00:33.038
Spot three weak lines in your draft: who, promise, and call to action.

00:00:33.038 --> 00:00:35.625
Remember the objective: fix three weak lines.

00:00:35.625 --> 00:00:39.692
Write the idea in your own words before you move on.

00:00:39.692 --> 00:00:44.127
Name one concrete next action you can finish in under an hour.

00:00:44.127 --> 00:00:48.194
Avoid vanity work that feels busy but does not create proof.

00:00:48.194 --> 00:00:52.630
If something is unclear, simplify the promise and try a smaller version.

00:00:52.630 --> 00:00:55.217
Talk to a real person when possible.

00:00:55.217 --> 00:00:56.696
Feedback beats guessing alone.

00:00:57.016 --> 00:01:00.765
Fix each line so a stranger could buy without guessing.

